---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hack Night — A place to keep building at Purdue"
  description="Hack Night is Purdue Hackers’ weekly gathering for personal projects in software, hardware, and design. Find collaborators, share progress, and keep building."
>
  <main
    class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-36 pb-24 font-polysans leading-relaxed"
  >
    <a href="/" class="font-inconsolata underline">← Purdue Hackers</a>
    <h1 class="font-pixel-hackers text-5xl md:text-7xl leading-tight mt-8 mb-8">
      Hack Night
    </h1>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">What is Hack Night?</h2>
    <p>
      Hack Night is Purdue Hackers’ weekly gathering for people working on
      personal projects across software, hardware, and design. Bring an idea,
      meet collaborators, join a session, or share work in progress at
      Checkpoints. You can return week after week as your project develops.
    </p>
    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
        When and where does Hack Night happen?
      </h2>
      <p>
        We meet on Fridays starting at 8 pm. The current location is
        <a class="underline" href="https://engineering.purdue.edu/HIVE"
          >the HIVE (BHEE 270/280)</a
        >
        at Purdue in West Lafayette, Indiana. The night ends when the last person
        leaves. Check the <a
          class="underline"
          href="https://events.purduehackers.com/">event calendar</a
        >
        for each week’s venue, sessions, and any schedule changes.
      </p>
      <p class="font-inconsolata text-sm mt-3">
        Location checked <time datetime="2026-10-20">October 20, 2026</time>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
        Is Purdue Hackers a hackathon?
      </h2>
      <p>
        Purdue Hackers is a community that supports people and their projects
        throughout the year. If you’re looking for a weekend event with a fixed
        deadline, a hackathon may fit. If you want a regular place to develop an
        ambitious idea, find collaborators, and keep going between events, Hack
        Night is for you. You can take part in both.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
        Do I need experience or a finished project?
      </h2>
      <p>
        If you go to Purdue, you’re invited—whether you’re new to coding or
        highly technical, an art major or a CS major. Bring your curiosity. At
        <a
          class="underline"
          href="https://blog.purduehackers.com/posts/how-we-cracked-demos"
          >Checkpoints</a
        >, people share progress, including work that’s still taking shape.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
        Where can I get support for an ambitious student project?
      </h2>
      <p>
        At Purdue, our <a
          class="underline"
          href="https://grants.purduehackers.com/">µgrants</a
        >
        program offers up to $1,000 for student projects and artworks. Hack Night
        brings you together with other builders. You can share progress on
        <a class="underline" href="https://ships.purduehackers.com/">Ships</a> and
        explore past <a
          class="underline"
          href="https://spill.purduehackers.com/">exhibitions</a
        >
        and <a class="underline" href="https://bento.purduehackers.com/"
          >talks</a
        >
        to see how people share their work with a wider audience. Check µgrants for
        current application availability.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">What have people built here?</h2>
      <p>
        See what people are making on
        <a class="underline" href="https://ships.purduehackers.com/">Ships</a>,
        browse projects from
        <a class="underline" href="https://burst.purduehackers.com/">BURST</a>
        and <a class="underline" href="https://spill.purduehackers.com/">spill</a>,
        or watch the <a class="underline" href="https://bento.purduehackers.com/"
          >BENTO talks</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
    <a class="join-session-btn mt-10" href="https://discord.gg/5paFjKzdPE"
      >Join our Discord ↗</a
    >
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
